hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1783","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears by Lat and Uzza should (renew his faith and) say La ilaha illallah, and whoever says to his companion, 'Come, let us gamble,' should give charity (as expiation for his sin)."
